    "updated_at": "2020-08-01T08:01:27Z",
    "body": "Hmm, actually because the table is increased in size to fit rowspans [at the end of each row group](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/tables.html#algorithm-for-ending-a-row-group) it's possible that this rowspan=2 element is just squashed back down by the layout algorithm. I'm not sure if there's any observable difference due to this, then? It might be worth rewriting the algorithm to not do this, either way.",
